WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.020
Yuma, this is dangerous!

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.720
It’s fine. We’re just passing through.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.690
It’s better to take
the long way around!

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.780
We ran into a dead end, but we shouldn’t
walk through a construction site.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.250
Yuma, what happens
at a construction site?

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.710
You don’t know?

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.020
It’s... umm...

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.350
A site to do construction!

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.110
Yuma, let’s go back!

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.380
Hurry up!

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.180
Kotori!

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.570
Why is it coming after us?

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.140
Jump!

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.880
Are you okay, Kotori?

00:00:58.880 --> 00:00:59.940
Yeah.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.700
What just happened?

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.610
No one was driving!

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.050
What?

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.780
Damn it!

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.090
You’re not even wearing helmets!

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:14.720
You shouldn’t be here!

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:21.470
Damn, I couldn’t stop it because my legs
aren’t long enough to reach the brakes.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.940
The driver was
an elementary school student?

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:24.930
What?

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:31.610
Elementary school? Shobe Yuatsu is in middle school, dammit!

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.040
Oh, you’re the same as us.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.110
I’m Kotori Mizuki. This is Yuma.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.700
Thank you for saving us, Shobe.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.870
Damn it!

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.780
That’s a large truck.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.130
It can carry
300 tons of dirt.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.970
300 tons? Wow!

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.310
No, not that type of “ton.” (“Ton” is another name for “pig” in Japanese.)

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.560
That crawler crane
can lift 750 tons.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.160
It can easily lift a rocket.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.980
Really? Wow!

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:12.980
Look at that.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.740
That six-sided piece.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:21.740
They use those tiny pieces
to connect the parts together.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.300
It’s incredible!

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.950
Yeah, right?

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.170
Boys really like this stuff.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:33.170
I want to operate it.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.450
Same here!

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:41.640
That’s why I’m participating
in the Duel Carnival.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:48.410
Even though I’m physically small,
I can use power shovel and crane monsters during a duel.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.370
I can become one with them.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.820
I know how you feel.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.880
You’re also in the Duel Carnival?

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:57.770
Yeah!

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:03.780
I see. But nobody can defeat my powerful Heavy Industry deck.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.740
My deck also
has plenty of power!

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.710
In that case, wanna battle?

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.710
Yeah, let’s duel!

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.710
Here I go!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.630
Duel Disk set!

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.590
D-Gazer set!

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.560
AR Vision Link complete.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.070
Duel target locked on!

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.020
Duel!

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:36.400
The strongest duelists from around
the world have gathered for the World Duel Carnival!

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.240
I need five Heart Pieces
to make it past the preliminaries!

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.530
Right now, I have
two Heart Pieces.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:46.490
I’m gonna make the finals
and win it all!

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.960
I reached my hand towards

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:54.140
The light that shines to tomorrow

00:03:54.140 --> 00:04:01.090
I dreamed of the world
that spreads beneath my feet

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:10.350
I don’t know where dreams
and hope are located

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:14.940
No matter how much I search,
I can’t find them

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.990
Maybe it fell into
the space between truth and lies

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:26.160
Our story hasn’t started yet

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:31.490
The road to tomorrow
seems like it will crumble

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:37.040
But let’s go
before we lose heart

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.130
As we come closer,
it moves further away

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.880
In order to seize the truth

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:48.510
We’ll search for hope
in the unseen future

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:51.230
Our hearts are stronger
than everyone else’s

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:54.510
We’ll carry it
within us and go

00:04:54.510 --> 00:05:00.110
Fight weakness to have
the strength to win

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.320
In order to find it

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.820
Along with my irreplaceable friends

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:12.050
I saw tomorrow in the world
that spreads beneath my feet

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.500
I’ll go first!

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:26.720
\hConstruction Site Duel! Defeat the Heavy Machinery Deck!!\h

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:26.720
Number 28:

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.980
My turn! I draw!

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:28.880
I summon Jumbo Drill!

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:40.880
I activate the spell card
Charging Construction!

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.490
When I summon a Heavy
Industry monster this turn...

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:49.120
I can Special Summon another Heavy Industry monster
from my hand in defense position this turn.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:54.590
I Special Summon Road
Roller in defense position!

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.920
I activate Jumbo Drill’s effect!

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:05.370
It gains 300 ATK for every Heavy
Industry monster on its team!

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:08.660
Heavy Industry monsters are cool!

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.930
This isn’t the time for that.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.700
Your opponent summoned two monsters.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.810
I set one card and end my turn!

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:22.950
I’ll show you the power
of my Heavy Industry deck!

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:26.740
My turn! I draw!

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.740
I summon Gagaga Magician!

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.200
I’m counting on you, Gagaga Magician!

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:40.470
Yuma, he has a monster with 2100 ATK
and another with 2100 DEF.

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:44.680
What can you do with Gagaga Magician
since it only has 1500 ATK?

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:45.880
Oh yeah!

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.630
This is bad!

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.550
Use an Equip Spell.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.340
Oh yeah.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:55.850
I activate the Equip Spell
Bound Wand from my hand!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:03.060
The equipped monster gains ATK equal
to its Level multiplied by 100.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.350
That’s only 1900 points.

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:08.490
It’s not powered up
enough to hurt me.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:10.990
Yuma.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:17.780
Once per turn, Gagaga Magician can
change its Level between 1 and 8.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:20.120
That’s right!

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.420
I activate Gagaga Magician’s effect!

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:26.920
I change it from Level 4 to 8,
so it gains 400 more points!

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:31.130
Due to Bound Wand’s effect,
it has 2300 ATK.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.890
Not bad!

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:37.920
Gagaga Magician attacks Jumbo Drill!

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:45.820
Not bad, but I activate
the trap card Foreman’s Fury!

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:53.820
When my Machine-Type monster battles,
your monster loses 1000 ATK.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.410
What?

00:07:58.410 --> 00:07:59.410
Destroy it!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.260
Yuma!

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.470
Use Bound Wand’s effect!

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.640
I know!

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:25.150
When the monster equipped with Bound Wand is destroyed
in battle, I can Special Summon that monster after battle.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:28.550
But that’s not enough
to change the situation.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.610
Focus on defense.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:35.110
If it’s in defense position, you
won’t take battle damage even if it’s destroyed.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:39.930
Understood! I Special Summon
Gagaga Magician in defense position!

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:46.170
I set one card
and end my turn.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:50.590
Do you really think that you
can defend against my power?

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.880
My turn! I draw!

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:58.010
I summon Strong Shovel Excavator!

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:09.290
Since I have another Heavy Industry monster,
Jumbo Drill gains 300 more ATK!

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.900
Strong Shovel Excavator attacks Gagaga Magician!

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:16.530
Yuma!

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:19.620
I activate the trap
card Half Unbreak!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:34.510
One of my monsters isn’t destroyed in battle,
and I take only half the damage.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:37.220
Furthermore, Gagaga Magician
is in defense position.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:42.620
That means both you
and your monster aren’t hurt this turn.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:47.440
But cheap tricks are pointless
against my Heavy Industry’s power!

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.990
I can still use Half
Unbreak’s effect!

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:55.610
Jumbo Drill attacks Gagaga Magician!

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.160
Jumbo Drill’s effect activates!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.870
When Jumbo Drill attacks
a monster in defense position...

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:10.710
...if it has more ATK than your monster’s DEF,
you take the difference as damage!

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.350
See that?

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:25.320
Powerful Heavy Industry monsters have high output,
gas mileage, durability and potential!

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:28.260
Huh? It’s now in defense position?

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.990
Well, umm...

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:37.800
When Jumbo Drill attacks, it switches
and stays in defense position until the end of my next turn.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:40.030
Dammit.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:42.980
In other words,
it’s out of commission?

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:47.930
Heavy-duty vehicles require maintenance
to unleash its full power.

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:50.830
That’s why I’m cooling
down the engine.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.090
This is your chance, Yuma.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.430
My turn! I draw!

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:58.380
I’m coming at ya!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.500
I switch Gagaga Magician
to attack position!

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:05.240
Then I summon Mystical Donator!

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:14.520
Once per turn, if I lower
Mystical Donator’s ATK to 0...

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:19.990
I can either have one monster
gains 800 ATK or regain 800 LP!

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:27.700
I activate Mystical Donator’s effect
to increase Gagaga Magician’s ATK by 800!

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:28.660
What?

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:32.420
Gagaga Magician attacks Strong Shovel Excavator!

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:43.210
I set one card
and end my turn!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:48.710
Gagaga Magician and Mystical
Donator’s ATK return to normal.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.450
I won’t lose against
your Heavy Industry power!

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:54.860
Dueling isn’t just about power!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.200
I see.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.590
Then what else is it?

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:02.810
Umm... You know... That.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:03.880
That?

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:06.710
Anyway, it’s just not about power!

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:08.590
What?

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:11.180
How can you win without power?

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:14.000
Whoever has the power is stronger!

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.640
Shobe?

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:18.830
It was during elementary school.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:24.610
I was the smallest in my class and physically weak,
so everyone made fun of me.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:27.140
Dammit, it wasn’t fun.

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:30.460
If I only had more power...

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:33.600
That’s when I discovered heavy-duty vehicles.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:43.060
I knew that if I had the power of the heavy-duty vehicles,
no one will make fun of me again.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:51.870
I’ll use the incredible power of my Heavy
Industry monsters to win the Carnival!

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.440
Shobe.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.150
Shobe...

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.710
My turn! I draw!

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:03.140
I activate the spell
card Scrap and Build!

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:09.190
I can Special Summon one Level 3-or-below
Machine-Type monster from my graveyard!

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:11.980
Resurrect, Strong Shovel Excavator!

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:16.650
When it’s Special Summoned
from my graveyard, it gains 1 Level.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:21.270
Next, I activate
the spell card Overhaul!

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:28.410
Overhaul increases the Level of all
Machine-Type monsters on my field by 1!

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:41.590
I’ll show you enormous power!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.200
It’s coming, Yuma.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:49.510
I overlay Level 5 Jumbo Drill,
Road Roller and Strong Shovel Excavator!

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:54.510
With these three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:56.440
Xyz Summon!

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:58.770
The steel arm that pulverizes stone!

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:02.610
Come out, my Xyz Monster!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.520
Digvorzhak, King of Heavy Industry!

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:10.810
3200 ATK?

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:16.440
It’s humongous!

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:22.380
This is my Xyz Monster Digvorzhak,
King of Heavy Industry!

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.440
Yuma, don’t let your guard down.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:25.050
Yeah.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.550
I activate Digvorzhak’s effect!

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:36.180
By using one Overlay Unit, Digvorzhak sends
three cards in your deck to the graveyard.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.810
I lost cards from my deck!

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:46.490
For every monster that this effect sent to the graveyard,
one of your monsters is destroyed!

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:50.240
What? Two monster cards
were sent to the graveyard!

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:53.450
That means two monsters are destroyed!

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.160
Take this! Mountain Crusher!

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:12.510
All of Yuma’s monsters are destroyed.

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:16.140
If I take a direct
attack, I’ll lose.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:17.680
Stay calm, Yuma. You should-

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:20.600
All right, Digvorzhak! Full throttle!

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:27.030
Sheesh, it’s so noisy!

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.320
..ap!

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:32.780
What did you say?
I can’t hear you!

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:36.370
Rev up the engine more!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:40.040
Digvorzhak, take away Yuma’s LP!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:43.290
...ap! Tr... is
what you need to use!

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.250
Aptr? What’s an aptr?

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:50.670
Go! Ultimate Bucket Wheel!

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:58.630
A trap!

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:05.150
I activate the trap
card Small Resistance!

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:13.450
Small Resistance lets me select one Level 4-or-below
monster in my graveyard with 1000-or-fewer ATK.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:20.580
Your monster loses ATK equal
to the selected monster’s ATK this turn!

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:25.980
Mystical Donator, I’m counting on you
to lower Digvorzhak’s ATK!

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.170
Yuma!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:36.390
Fear my superior power!
I end my turn!

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:42.120
I managed to survive,
but I only have 100 LP left.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:46.650
I don’t have a monster
that can face 3200 ATK.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.730
Yuma, look at that.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:56.530
That... of... is...

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.440
I can’t hear you!

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:01.350
It’s going to end like this?

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:03.750
Yes, if you’re fighting alone.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.680
What?

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:09.280
Hey, why can I hear you?

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:13.220
We’re talking with our hearts.

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:15.180
I see.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:21.080
I’ve observed many things today
at this construction site.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:27.650
I learned that humans create gigantic
buildings by connecting various parts.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.510
So what?

00:17:29.510 --> 00:17:33.110
There’s a six-sided
piece by your foot.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.070
It’s just a nut.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:43.790
That six-sided piece is a very tiny piece,
but it supports this large building.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.300
It’s the same in a duel.

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:50.210
Tiny parts support a large building...

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:55.870
Power isn’t everything.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.560
What’s wrong, Yuma?

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:05.350
I knew you couldn’t do anything against
the superior power of my Digvorzhak.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.980
My turn! I draw!

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.150
All right, it’s here!

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:12.480
I summon Kurivolt!

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.820
300 ATK?

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:23.950
You can’t do anything
with that low emission monster!

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:27.040
I activate Kurivolt’s effect!

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:35.010
Digvorzhak’s Overlay Units!

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:40.390
The effect changes Overlay Units
into Kurivolt Tokens!

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:46.310
What? It changes Overlay Units
into monsters? Damn it!

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:51.360
But three weak monsters can’t
do anything against Digvorzhak.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:55.070
I activate the spell card Mini-Guts!

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.930
Go, Kurivolt Tokens!

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:15.750
What can you do
with those weak monsters?

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:26.180
What’s wrong, Digvorzhak?

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:42.030
By tributing two Level 1 monsters,
the spell card Mini-Guts makes your monster have 0 ATK.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:46.200
Digvorzhak is...

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.910
Why? Those monsters are weak!

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.680
Let’s finish this, Yuma.

00:19:51.680 --> 00:19:54.880
Yeah! I’m kattobing!

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:59.090
Kurivolt attacks Digvorzhak!

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:22.610
Damn it!

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:27.920
Mini-Guts also deals damage equal
to the destroyed Digvorzhak’s original ATK!

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:34.000
In other words, you take
3200 points of damage!

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:37.170
Your power backfired!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.840
All right!

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:58.680
Why?

00:20:58.680 --> 00:21:02.150
Why did I lose against
a weak-powered monster?

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:05.610
You shouldn’t underestimate small powers.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.310
Small power?

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:13.620
Nuts and bolts support large
bridges or this building.

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:22.810
I lose.

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:26.270
You get my Heart Piece, damn it.

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:29.420
I accept.

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:32.680
Now you have three pieces.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:37.190
Like you said, I forgot
about something important.

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:41.650
Building large objects
require more than large power.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:44.910
Shobe, even though
you’re small, you’re cool.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:49.560
Well...

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:54.770
Small power.

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:56.810
Hey!

00:21:56.810 --> 00:22:00.170
What are you doing here?

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:04.050
You can get hurt!

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:07.220
We’re sorry!

00:22:19.930 --> 00:22:23.090
Someone gave me water

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:28.990
It easily created a rainbow

00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:34.930
To be
who I want to be

00:22:35.730 --> 00:22:37.960
Is difficult

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:41.670
Without struggle

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:45.630
I can’t win

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:48.430
But I want to bloom

00:22:48.960 --> 00:22:52.470
I have a dream
that’s not cool

00:22:52.860 --> 00:22:55.930
In order to achieve it

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:59.370
I don’t care
if you laugh at me

00:22:59.370 --> 00:23:06.530
I set my limits low

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:09.820
So I’ll overcome it tomorrow

00:23:09.820 --> 00:23:13.410
Ah! Aiming for the blue skies

00:23:13.970 --> 00:23:15.330
In full bloom

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:17.560
Yearning freesia

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:23.100
Countless petals

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:25.960
Were sacrificed

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:29.510
I’m above them

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:34.220
Ah! Lost my way again today

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:35.770
I admire

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:37.560
Yearning freesia

00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:45.150
A stranger attacked me during
the Duel Carnival.

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:48.820
And she keeps coming after me!

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:50.150
Yuma, isn’t she...

00:23:50.710 --> 00:23:54.320
I don’t remember who she is!

00:23:54.320 --> 00:23:57.290
Don’t underestimate her dueling.

00:23:57.290 --> 00:24:01.460
I don’t know what’s going on,
but I won’t lose a duel!

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:07.330
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“The Railroad Deck Takes Off! The Rowdy Duelist, Anna”

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:10.050
\h\hThe Railroad Deck Takes Off! The Rowdy Duelist, Anna\h\h

00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:09.550
I’m kattobing!

00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:13.180
Is kattobing good for you physically?

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:18.810
Yeah! It helps you when you’re
depressed, nervous or angry!

00:24:18.810 --> 00:24:20.730
Those are all emotional issues!

00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:24.550
Let’s all kattobing!
